readme = f"""# Source facit that can be connected to the correct dental query\n\nThe idea is to maintain number, drive, locator, population, protocol, resolution and time together. Then we can determine which source actually limits a downstream result. All six The swarm reports have now been reviewed. Delivery is a `information_link` draft with {N} observationsbuntar, {K} fields; and {P} mottagarportar; `PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW`.\n\nRun from this directory:\n\n```sh\n./run_all.sh\n```\n\nIt recreates table arithmetic, error checks, figures, six job reports and FACIT.csv offline. System-Python, SciPy and Matplotlib are needed. A thread, approximately {x['cost']['maxrss_KiB'] / 1024:.0f} MiB RAM, no GPU. The overrun does not change the originals of the receiver. The only new expansion draft is `raw/SOURCE_DRAFT.jsonl` ; when replaying, its exchange must match the frozen source contracts.\n\n| Question | Result and external reference | Followed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Which group has 443.7 N? | Women with prostheses, n=107. Without prosthesis: 818,6 N , n=179 . [Yoshikawa Table 3 ](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13168838/). PER_ARCH/POPULATION. | The swarm's group label is fixed. No parade tooth/height intervention. |\n| Can the force regions form a partition? | Printed means 14,3 + 50,1 + 43,9 = 108,3 %. [Table 2](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5509719/). PER_SURFACE_REGION/POPULATION. | Shared partition rejected. |\n| Is 0,136 a ICC estimate? | No: ICC 0,653, KI 0,136–0,866. [Diagnostics Table 2](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8700671/). PER_ARCH / POPULATION ; dimensionless. | Error column fixed; no mm - boundary for canal wall . |\n| Is Grunheid's numbers repeatability? | The harvest uses the accuracy table and loses minus signs. [Primary PDF , page 160 , Table II / III ](https://www.dentsplysirona.com/content/dam/master/education/documents/upload/S/Study%201%20Accuracy%2C%20reproducibility%2C%20and%20efficiency.pdf). PER_TOOTH/POPULATION. | Table, characters and MSE unit mm² are reset. |\n| Is there a real deflection factor? | Yes: X − 38,99 to 39,34 µm , Y − 41 to 41,81 µm . [Mamedov primary PDF , pages 149 – 150 ](https://cdm21054.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/api/collection/IR/id/8108/download). PER_POINT. | New benchmark protocol for X89 : WC 1,5 mm / Al7050 , 20 000 rpm, ap 300 µm , feeding 20 µm / tooth . Laser 1 mm from the tip, then extrapolation. |\n| Can late RCT case replace intraoperative conversion? | 3 / 47 after trauma, 25 / 86 intraoperatively in caries. [Li Table 2 / 4 ](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13535951/), [Patel Table 4 + flow rate](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11629050/). POPULATION. | Different time outputs/denominators; not poolable. |\n| Is 0,5 mm all zirconia's wall requirements? | [KATANA page 5](https://www.kuraraynoritake.com/world/product/cad_materials/pdf/katana_zircinia_technical_guide.pdf): ML/HT anterior/posterior 0,4/0,5, UTML/STML 0,8/1,0 mm. PER_POINT specifikation. | Material scenarios change the sub-output of the wall. No demonstrated full crown shape pass of 72 saved candidates . |\n\n[Refound deflection measurement and correct ICC - column ](FIGURE_R4.png)\n\nWhat does not holds : no new empirical interval or frozen main decision of the seven recipients can be replaced by these sources . Mamedov's experiments have different tool geometry/material regimen than X89 and lack tabulated paired force displacement points; no 1 N stiffness is derived. The average distance of the channel centre lines is not signed local channel wall loss. Pooled KI, SE and Patient Agents- SD must not become individual implant - SD. Symmetrics and six cup points do not calibrate complete crown's surface-reaweighted P95. Li also has conflicting tables.\n\n{D}/{A} named entries ({100 * D / A:.1f} %) has no exported certified numerical bundle. Two manufacturer specifications are added separately. Source access is separated: saved primary XML / PDF , abstract, indexed primary text and clearly marked browser transcriptions. A transcription shash authenticates our reading note, not the original of the publication. Numerical presence in text does not prove the correct table column or scientific interpretation.\n\n{x['verification']['contract_injections_rejected']} injected errors are dropped in the frozen contract; five separate table checks and 18 guide controls can also reject error values. This tests integrity/aritemetics. The manual source review needs an independent reviewer. Adequate witnesses have identity error exactly 0 but downstream differences 1,125 and 2 mm respectively; custom mathematical designs, not dental reference . No affinity sensitivity is reported; rigorous floating point enclosure for geometry and numerical quantiles are missing.\n\nData/licence: only local article texts and hashade aggregate recipient snapshots are read. No new patient images, mesh datasets or zip cases are included. [SOURCE_LICENSES.json ](SOURCE_LICENSES.json) specifies license per source document. Mamedov's original CC BY - NC - ND , Gurian's manuscript CC BY 4.0 ; for manufacturer/grunheid-PDF the resale right is not established. The originals are local review material. Geometric snapshots underlying dataset licenses belong to each recipient; no new mesh data is distributed.\n\n[RESULTS.md ](RESULTS.md) gives all recipient decisions and conversions; `JOB_*.md` provides each locator and reason for rejection. [FACIT.csv ](FACIT.csv), [CONSUMER_PORTS.json ](CONSUMER_PORTS.json), [results.json ](results.json) and [HANDOFF.md ](HANDOFF.md) are auditable deliveries. Figures are also available as PDF .\n"""
